1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,344
It's six thirty in the morning.

2
00:00:02,244 --> 00:00:04,100
Your alarm goes off... once.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,707
And you actually get up.

4
00:00:05,907 --> 00:00:07,529
No snooze. No panic.

5
00:00:07,429 --> 00:00:09,660
No racing heart. Just... up.

6
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,997
You even have time to make the bed.

7
00:00:12,347 --> 00:00:15,071
Across town, Jake's alarm goes off at

8
00:00:14,971 --> 00:00:16,489
the exact same time.

9
00:00:16,689 --> 00:00:18,953
He hits snooze. Then again. And again.

10
00:00:19,153 --> 00:00:21,499
Every nine minutes, the same little fight

11
00:00:21,399 --> 00:00:22,321
with his phone.

12
00:00:22,521 --> 00:00:24,768
And every time, he tells himself...

13
00:00:24,668 --> 00:00:26,180
just five more minutes.

14
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:28,469
By the time he opens his eyes

15
00:00:28,369 --> 00:00:30,181
for real, it's eight fifty.

16
00:00:30,381 --> 00:00:32,078
His meeting starts at nine.

17
00:00:32,278 --> 00:00:35,009
He's late. Again. Third time this month.

18
00:00:35,359 --> 00:00:37,559
And here's the thing nobody tells you.

19
00:00:37,759 --> 00:00:40,238
Jake's messy morning isn't just stressful.

20
00:00:40,438 --> 00:00:42,043
It's costing him money.

21
00:00:41,943 --> 00:00:43,940
Real money. Every single day.

22
00:00:44,139 --> 00:00:46,609
Not in one big painful moment.

23
00:00:46,509 --> 00:00:48,662
In tiny, invisible pieces.

24
00:00:49,012 --> 00:00:50,992
Stay with me, because by the end

25
00:00:50,892 --> 00:00:53,459
of this story you'll see exactly how much.

26
00:00:53,659 --> 00:00:56,090
And the simple morning routine that makes

27
00:00:55,990 --> 00:00:57,795
you calmer, more productive...

28
00:00:57,995 --> 00:01:01,539
and about three thousand dollars richer every single year.

29
00:01:01,889 --> 00:01:04,130
So let's rewind. Let's go back to

30
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:05,233
the night before.

31
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:07,944
Because a good morning doesn't actually start

32
00:01:07,844 --> 00:01:08,747
in the morning.

33
00:01:08,947 --> 00:01:11,773
It starts around nine thirty the evening before.

34
00:01:11,973 --> 00:01:13,932
Sounds boring? Stick with me.

35
00:01:13,832 --> 00:01:15,985
This is where the magic happens.

36
00:01:16,335 --> 00:01:18,369
You give it ten minutes. That's all.

37
00:01:18,569 --> 00:01:21,056
You lay out tomorrow's clothes on the chair.

38
00:01:21,255 --> 00:01:22,529
You pack your lunch.

39
00:01:22,429 --> 00:01:25,109
You fill the coffee maker and set the timer.

40
00:01:25,459 --> 00:01:28,125
Keys, wallet, badge... all in one little

41
00:01:28,025 --> 00:01:29,216
bowl by the door.

42
00:01:29,416 --> 00:01:31,416
It feels almost too simple, right?

43
00:01:31,616 --> 00:01:33,900
But every decision you make tonight is

44
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,140
one you don't have to make half asleep.

45
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:37,942
No searching. No stress.

46
00:01:37,842 --> 00:01:40,320
Everything is right where you left it.

47
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:42,504
And then you do one more thing.

48
00:01:42,404 --> 00:01:43,175
The big one.

49
00:01:43,375 --> 00:01:44,941
You plug your phone in...

50
00:01:44,841 --> 00:01:45,879
across the room.

51
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,306
Not on your pillow.

52
00:01:47,206 --> 00:01:48,314
Not in your hand.

53
00:01:48,214 --> 00:01:49,263
Across the room.

54
00:01:49,613 --> 00:01:52,098
Why? Because now, when the alarm rings,

55
00:01:51,998 --> 00:01:54,299
you have to stand up to turn it off.

56
00:01:54,499 --> 00:01:55,856
And once you're standing?

57
00:01:56,056 --> 00:01:58,673
Honestly... the hardest part of the morning

58
00:01:58,573 --> 00:01:59,610
is already over.

59
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,261
Meanwhile, Jake is in bed. Scrolling.

60
00:02:02,461 --> 00:02:05,215
Eleven thirty. Midnight. Twelve forty.

61
00:02:05,415 --> 00:02:07,561
One more video. Just one more.

62
00:02:07,761 --> 00:02:09,547
His brain is wide awake.

63
00:02:09,447 --> 00:02:11,654
His body is begging for sleep.

64
00:02:12,004 --> 00:02:14,106
Most adults need at least seven hours

65
00:02:14,006 --> 00:02:15,026
of sleep a night.

66
00:02:15,226 --> 00:02:16,545
Jake gets about six.

67
00:02:16,445 --> 00:02:18,190
And that's on a good night.

68
00:02:18,390 --> 00:02:20,511
He doesn't feel tired at midnight.

69
00:02:20,411 --> 00:02:21,759
He feels it at seven.

70
00:02:21,959 --> 00:02:24,495
So every morning starts with a little sleep debt.

71
00:02:24,845 --> 00:02:26,188
So the next morning,

72
00:02:26,088 --> 00:02:28,798
that snooze button feels like a lifesaver.

73
00:02:28,998 --> 00:02:30,448
Just nine more minutes.

74
00:02:30,348 --> 00:02:31,621
What could go wrong?

75
00:02:31,821 --> 00:02:33,406
But it isn't a lifesaver.

76
00:02:33,306 --> 00:02:34,119
It's a trap.

77
00:02:34,469 --> 00:02:37,464
Those extra minutes don't give you real, deep rest.

78
00:02:37,664 --> 00:02:39,193
You just drift in and out,

79
00:02:39,093 --> 00:02:39,908
in and out...

80
00:02:40,108 --> 00:02:42,663
and you wake up even groggier than before.

81
00:02:43,013 --> 00:02:44,672
And then the scramble begins.

82
00:02:44,872 --> 00:02:46,887
No clean shirt. No breakfast.

83
00:02:46,787 --> 00:02:48,603
Keys? Where are the keys?!

84
00:02:48,803 --> 00:02:51,279
He finds them in yesterday's jeans.

85
00:02:51,179 --> 00:02:52,161
On the floor.

86
00:02:52,361 --> 00:02:54,618
His heart is pounding before he even

87
00:02:54,518 --> 00:02:55,877
leaves the apartment.

88
00:02:56,227 --> 00:02:58,197
He runs out the door with nothing.

89
00:02:58,397 --> 00:02:59,921
No coffee. No food.

90
00:02:59,821 --> 00:03:01,419
No plan for the day.

91
00:03:01,619 --> 00:03:03,709
Just stress. And a growing headache.

92
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:06,815
And that's exactly where his wallet starts bleeding.

93
00:03:07,015 --> 00:03:09,704
Quietly. Politely. Every single morning.

94
00:03:09,904 --> 00:03:10,855
Watch this.

95
00:03:11,055 --> 00:03:12,233
And the worst part?

96
00:03:12,133 --> 00:03:14,275
He doesn't even notice it happening.

97
00:03:14,625 --> 00:03:17,628
Stop number one: the coffee shop on the corner.

98
00:03:17,828 --> 00:03:19,498
There's a line, of course.

99
00:03:19,398 --> 00:03:20,706
He's even later now.

100
00:03:20,906 --> 00:03:23,184
A large latte. Six dollars.

101
00:03:23,534 --> 00:03:25,978
Stop number two: a breakfast sandwich,

102
00:03:25,878 --> 00:03:27,335
because he's starving.

103
00:03:27,535 --> 00:03:29,652
He eats it in four bites, walking.

104
00:03:29,852 --> 00:03:30,829
Eight dollars.

105
00:03:31,179 --> 00:03:34,077
Fourteen dollars. Gone before nine A M.

106
00:03:34,277 --> 00:03:35,901
Does that sound like a lot?

107
00:03:36,101 --> 00:03:38,467
Not really, right? It's just breakfast.

108
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:41,310
And honestly, Jake would say the same thing.

109
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:43,145
But let's do the math.

110
00:03:43,045 --> 00:03:45,159
Fourteen dollars, every workday.

111
00:03:45,359 --> 00:03:47,375
About twenty one workdays a month.

112
00:03:47,575 --> 00:03:51,189
That's roughly two hundred ninety four dollars. Every month.

113
00:03:51,539 --> 00:03:52,705
Over a full year?

114
00:03:52,605 --> 00:03:55,340
About three thousand five hundred dollars.

115
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:59,352
Gone. On coffee and sandwiches he barely even tasted.

116
00:03:59,552 --> 00:04:02,636
That's a vacation. That's an emergency fund. Gone.

117
00:04:02,836 --> 00:04:04,483
Think about that for a second.

118
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:06,199
And you know what's worse?

119
00:04:06,399 --> 00:04:08,359
Jake isn't even enjoying it.

120
00:04:08,559 --> 00:04:10,121
He's eating at his desk,

121
00:04:10,021 --> 00:04:12,497
stressed, already behind on everything.

122
00:04:12,697 --> 00:04:14,350
By lunch, he's exhausted.

123
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:15,965
And he's buying lunch too.

124
00:04:16,315 --> 00:04:17,960
Now. Let's look at your morning.

125
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,857
Same city. Same job.

126
00:04:19,757 --> 00:04:21,615
Same paycheck as Jake.

127
00:04:21,815 --> 00:04:24,001
The only difference is what happens in

128
00:04:23,901 --> 00:04:25,374
the first thirty minutes.

129
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:27,349
You get up at six thirty.

130
00:04:27,249 --> 00:04:28,874
You walk across the room.

131
00:04:29,074 --> 00:04:30,656
You switch off the alarm.

132
00:04:30,856 --> 00:04:32,848
And then you do something that feels

133
00:04:32,748 --> 00:04:35,161
weird at first... you leave the phone there.

134
00:04:35,361 --> 00:04:37,698
No notifications. No headlines.

135
00:04:37,598 --> 00:04:39,573
Just you and a quiet room.

136
00:04:39,923 --> 00:04:42,340
Because the second you open your phone,

137
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,300
your morning isn't yours anymore.

138
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,369
Emails. News. Group chats.

139
00:04:46,269 --> 00:04:48,003
Other people's problems.

140
00:04:48,203 --> 00:04:50,089
You haven't even brushed your teeth,

141
00:04:49,989 --> 00:04:51,479
and you're already stressed.

142
00:04:51,829 --> 00:04:54,677
So instead, you drink a big glass of water.

143
00:04:54,877 --> 00:04:56,261
You open the window.

144
00:04:56,161 --> 00:04:57,545
Cold air. Fresh air.

145
00:04:57,745 --> 00:05:00,139
Five slow, deep breaths. That's it.

146
00:05:00,339 --> 00:05:01,782
Your body wakes up.

147
00:05:01,682 --> 00:05:03,267
Your mind slows down.

148
00:05:03,617 --> 00:05:05,561
Then you move. Just ten minutes.

149
00:05:05,761 --> 00:05:07,331
A walk around the block.

150
00:05:07,231 --> 00:05:09,844
A few stretches on the living room floor.

151
00:05:10,044 --> 00:05:11,903
Nothing fancy. No gym.

152
00:05:11,803 --> 00:05:13,022
No fancy gear.

153
00:05:13,372 --> 00:05:15,554
You're not training for a marathon here.

154
00:05:15,754 --> 00:05:17,720
You're just telling your body...

155
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:19,004
hey. It's daytime now.

156
00:05:19,204 --> 00:05:20,913
And by the time you get back,

157
00:05:20,813 --> 00:05:22,134
your head feels clear.

158
00:05:22,334 --> 00:05:24,937
Some mornings you even see the sunrise.

159
00:05:24,837 --> 00:05:26,926
Jake hasn't seen one in months.

160
00:05:27,276 --> 00:05:30,024
Back home, the coffee's already ready and waiting.

161
00:05:30,224 --> 00:05:32,756
Because you set it up last night. Remember?

162
00:05:32,956 --> 00:05:35,557
That smell. Honestly, it's the best part

163
00:05:35,457 --> 00:05:36,245
of the day.

164
00:05:36,595 --> 00:05:38,867
Coffee at home costs you about fifty

165
00:05:38,767 --> 00:05:39,591
cents a cup.

166
00:05:39,791 --> 00:05:41,388
Oatmeal with a banana?

167
00:05:41,288 --> 00:05:43,157
Maybe another fifty cents.

168
00:05:43,357 --> 00:05:45,730
So breakfast costs you about one dollar.

169
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:47,026
And you know what?

170
00:05:46,926 --> 00:05:49,296
It tastes better than the six dollar one.

171
00:05:49,646 --> 00:05:51,397
One dollar. Sitting down.

172
00:05:51,297 --> 00:05:53,179
Actually tasting your food.

173
00:05:53,379 --> 00:05:56,685
Versus Jake's fourteen dollar sprint down the sidewalk.

174
00:05:56,885 --> 00:05:59,170
Same caffeine. Same full stomach.

175
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:00,560
Very different price.

176
00:06:00,910 --> 00:06:03,640
And now comes the part that changes everything.

177
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:05,228
It takes ten minutes.

178
00:06:05,128 --> 00:06:06,822
And almost nobody does it.

179
00:06:07,022 --> 00:06:08,639
The ten minute money check.

180
00:06:08,989 --> 00:06:10,728
Now you pick up the phone.

181
00:06:10,628 --> 00:06:11,862
But only for this.

182
00:06:12,062 --> 00:06:14,085
Minute one: you look at your balance.

183
00:06:14,285 --> 00:06:15,863
No fear. No guessing.

184
00:06:15,763 --> 00:06:17,340
Just the real number.

185
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,445
Ten minutes. One cup of coffee.

186
00:06:19,345 --> 00:06:20,842
That's the whole system.

187
00:06:21,192 --> 00:06:23,054
Next: you check what came out of

188
00:06:22,954 --> 00:06:24,321
your account yesterday.

189
00:06:24,521 --> 00:06:27,548
Anything weird? A charge you don't recognize?

190
00:06:27,748 --> 00:06:30,116
Most days, it's nothing. But today...

191
00:06:30,466 --> 00:06:31,972
Today, you catch something.

192
00:06:32,172 --> 00:06:34,239
A free trial you forgot about.

193
00:06:34,139 --> 00:06:37,123
It just turned into a fifteen dollar charge.

194
00:06:37,323 --> 00:06:40,048
And it would've kept charging you. Every month.

195
00:06:40,248 --> 00:06:42,743
Fifteen dollars a month is one hundred

196
00:06:42,643 --> 00:06:44,130
eighty dollars a year.

197
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:47,048
You cancel it. Right there. Thirty seconds.

198
00:06:47,248 --> 00:06:49,176
Fifteen dollars a month, saved...

199
00:06:49,376 --> 00:06:51,412
before your coffee is even cold.

200
00:06:51,612 --> 00:06:54,002
If something's tight, you know today.

201
00:06:53,902 --> 00:06:54,869
Not on Friday.

202
00:06:55,219 --> 00:06:56,409
Then you look ahead.

203
00:06:56,609 --> 00:06:58,475
Which bills are due this week?

204
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:00,299
Rent? Phone? The electric bill?

205
00:07:00,499 --> 00:07:02,513
Is there enough money sitting there for

206
00:07:02,413 --> 00:07:03,102
all of them?

207
00:07:03,302 --> 00:07:04,764
He didn't lack the money.

208
00:07:04,664 --> 00:07:05,854
He just didn't look.

209
00:07:06,204 --> 00:07:07,816
Jake never does this.

210
00:07:08,016 --> 00:07:11,190
Last month, he completely forgot his electric bill.

211
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:13,096
Late fee. Thirty dollars.

212
00:07:12,996 --> 00:07:14,573
For absolutely nothing.

213
00:07:14,923 --> 00:07:16,823
You? You haven't paid a late fee

214
00:07:16,723 --> 00:07:17,667
in over a year.

215
00:07:17,867 --> 00:07:20,124
Because you see every bill coming...

216
00:07:20,024 --> 00:07:21,322
days before it hits.

217
00:07:21,522 --> 00:07:24,352
No surprises. No panic. No fees.

218
00:07:24,702 --> 00:07:26,808
And then, the last part of your morning.

219
00:07:27,008 --> 00:07:28,638
You open a little notebook.

220
00:07:28,838 --> 00:07:30,390
And you pick your top three.

221
00:07:30,590 --> 00:07:32,314
Small list. Big days.

222
00:07:32,664 --> 00:07:35,093
Not a to-do list with twenty things

223
00:07:34,993 --> 00:07:37,023
on it. Nobody finishes those.

224
00:07:37,223 --> 00:07:38,239
Just three.

225
00:07:38,439 --> 00:07:40,774
The three things that would make today

226
00:07:40,674 --> 00:07:43,008
a win, even if nothing else gets done.

227
00:07:43,208 --> 00:07:46,138
Because willpower is strongest in the morning.

228
00:07:46,038 --> 00:07:47,552
Use it on what matters.

229
00:07:47,902 --> 00:07:49,205
And the hardest one?

230
00:07:49,105 --> 00:07:50,166
You do it first.

231
00:07:50,366 --> 00:07:52,625
Before the emails. Before the meetings.

232
00:07:52,525 --> 00:07:53,954
Before the noise starts.

233
00:07:54,154 --> 00:07:55,919
While your brain is still fresh.

234
00:07:56,269 --> 00:07:57,125
By ten A M,

235
00:07:57,025 --> 00:07:59,945
your most important work is already done.

236
00:08:00,145 --> 00:08:03,476
And Jake? He's still answering emails from yesterday.

237
00:08:03,676 --> 00:08:06,425
Still on his second coffee. Still behind.

238
00:08:06,625 --> 00:08:08,380
Not because you work longer.

239
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,741
Because you work first.

240
00:08:10,091 --> 00:08:12,608
Your boss notices. Of course she does.

241
00:08:12,808 --> 00:08:14,057
You're the calm one.

242
00:08:13,957 --> 00:08:16,241
The one who actually gets things done.

243
00:08:16,441 --> 00:08:17,884
And people like that...

244
00:08:17,784 --> 00:08:19,519
tend to get the raise first.

245
00:08:19,869 --> 00:08:21,259
So let's do the math.

246
00:08:21,159 --> 00:08:22,488
Just the money part.

247
00:08:22,688 --> 00:08:25,364
Jake spends about three thousand five hundred

248
00:08:25,264 --> 00:08:27,310
dollars a year on rushed mornings.

249
00:08:27,510 --> 00:08:29,669
You spend about two hundred fifty on

250
00:08:29,569 --> 00:08:30,698
breakfast at home.

251
00:08:31,048 --> 00:08:32,029
The difference?

252
00:08:32,229 --> 00:08:35,710
Three thousand two hundred seventy six dollars. Every year.

253
00:08:35,910 --> 00:08:38,770
That's about two hundred seventy three dollars

254
00:08:38,670 --> 00:08:41,051
a month, moved into savings on payday.

255
00:08:41,251 --> 00:08:43,432
Little things. Every single morning.

256
00:08:43,782 --> 00:08:46,104
And that's without counting the late fees

257
00:08:46,004 --> 00:08:46,863
you never pay.

258
00:08:47,063 --> 00:08:48,936
Without the free trials you catch.

259
00:08:49,136 --> 00:08:50,613
And without the stress...

260
00:08:50,513 --> 00:08:52,595
which you can't even put a price on.

261
00:08:52,945 --> 00:08:54,704
Now fast forward one year.

262
00:08:54,904 --> 00:08:56,874
Jake is still running out the door

263
00:08:56,774 --> 00:08:57,700
at eight fifty.

264
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:01,022
Still tired. Still buying the fourteen dollar

265
00:09:00,922 --> 00:09:03,239
breakfast. Still broke by Friday.

266
00:09:03,439 --> 00:09:05,053
Calm mornings. Every day.

267
00:09:04,953 --> 00:09:06,083
For a whole year.

268
00:09:06,433 --> 00:09:08,879
You? You've got over three thousand dollars

269
00:09:08,779 --> 00:09:09,915
sitting in savings.

270
00:09:10,115 --> 00:09:12,258
From mornings. Just... mornings.

271
00:09:12,458 --> 00:09:13,771
You didn't earn more.

272
00:09:13,671 --> 00:09:15,908
You didn't give up anything you love.

273
00:09:16,108 --> 00:09:17,798
Start there. Tomorrow morning,

274
00:09:17,698 --> 00:09:19,229
you'll feel the difference.

275
00:09:19,579 --> 00:09:22,069
You just stopped letting your mornings happen to you.

276
00:09:22,269 --> 00:09:24,228
So tonight, try just one thing.

277
00:09:24,428 --> 00:09:25,832
Lay out your clothes.

